# Dark Factory Harness — secrets and endpoints
#
# Copy to .env and fill in what the profiles you actually use require:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored. Never paste a key into harness.config.json, a prompt file,
# a WP log or a commit message. A profile declares what it needs in env_required,
# and /df-implementer --smoke fails loudly when one is missing — which is the point:
# a missing key should stop you at 23:00, not surface as a 401 at 3am.
#
# Profiles that need nothing here: codex-cloud (uses `codex login`) and every local
# profile (lmstudio, ollama). Running the model on your own machine means there is
# no key to leak and no per-token bill.

# --- OpenRouter -------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed by: opencode-openrouter, codex-openrouter
# Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: direct provider keys ------------------------------------------
# Only if you add a profile that talks to one of these directly.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: endpoint overrides --------------------------------------------
# Defaults are the standard local ports; set these only if you moved them.
# A profile's preflight.check and its OpenCode config file must agree with whatever you put here.
# LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
